{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"936ac7541000db4f9937d8d733cb19c5ace817ec9d77ac25d857825b88329351","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM/Bedrock provider region resolution","key_entities":["build_bedrock_provider","resolve_bedrock_region","boto3.session.Session","REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION","AWS_DEFAULT_REGION","AWS_REGION","bedrock_model.py","capabilities.py","runner.py","provenance_for","provider_provenance","region_source"],"problem_keywords":["bedrock region resolution","AWS_REGION environment variable","region precedence","provider configuration"],"propositions":["bedrock provider ignores AWS_REGION environment variable and only consults REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION or AWS_DEFAULT_REGION, requiring manual injection of region config to run LLM operations","botocore does not resolve AWS_REGION, so rebar must implement its own resolver that chains REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION > AWS_DEFAULT_REGION > AWS_REGION before passing region_name explicitly to boto3.session.Session","region and region_source must be recorded in provider_provenance for bedrock runs when rebar's resolution chain succeeds, and omitted when profile-based fallback applies","error message must document the full resolution chain (REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION, AWS_DEFAULT_REGION, AWS_REGION, profile) and remove stale AWS_REGION-does-not-work guidance"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787316862910590001,"uuid":"78076c0c-b7fd-487e-9e74-96c5b7d1819d"}